    # v393 (14/10/2026) -- THE RULE AND THE HEART: three rule stones in the kernel, the operator's four inscriptions (verbatim, sha256), the real consumer with the rule and the heart seal; the numbers are READ
    # from the records pedras_v393, regra_consumidor_v393 and coracao_e_selo_gravitacional_v393 (which read them from the rite's own kernel and core). Nothing here moves the gate.
    _pd393 = core.get("pedras_v393") or {}
    _rc393 = core.get("regra_consumidor_v393") or {}
    _cr393 = core.get("coracao_e_selo_gravitacional_v393") or {}
    _cg393 = core.get("cunhagens_regra_v393") or {}
    _i393 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _f393 = lambda x_: (r"%.3e" % x_) if isinstance(x_, float) else r"n/a"
    _bf393 = _pd393.get("bandeiras") or [None, None]
    _dc393 = _pd393.get("declaracoes_no_trio") or [None, None]
    _el393 = _pd393.get("escada") or {}
    _nm393 = _rc393.get("numeros") or {}
    _sa393 = (_rc393.get("satisfacao") or {})
    _cr_sat393 = (_cr393.get("satisfacao_pela_regra") or {})
    _vb393 = _pd393.get("verbatim") or {}
    s.append(r"\section*{The rule and the heart (v393): the rule as the refusal that the result differ from the object of its satisfaction}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The rule and the heart (v393): the rule as the refusal that the result differ from the object of its satisfaction}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{This round the record did NOT seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if _pd393.get("all_verified") is not True else r"")
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} Three modules in the kernel, each with its sha256 pinned and checked at every rite against the embedded body: \texttt{RuleTruthContract} (the contract: admissibility relative to a reading and a target), "
             r"\texttt{TheRuleAndTheFigureOfTruth} (the realization, linked to \texttt{TheJudgedThing}, \texttt{TheNonMinimalCoupling}, \texttt{TheGeometricCostOfAbsoluteZero} and \texttt{TheLedgerOfCharges}) and "
             r"\texttt{TheRuleInTheContinuousMotor} (the rule linked to the continuous motor). Flags lit: " + _i393(_bf393[0]) + r" of " + _i393(_bf393[1])
             + r"; declarations audited with only the axioms $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$: " + _i393(_dc393[0]) + r" of " + _i393(_dc393[1])
             + r"; the kernel ladder reads " + _i393(_el393.get("limpos")) + r" of " + _i393(_el393.get("esperados")) + r" (it was " + _i393(_el393.get("da_v392")) + r" in v392). "
             r"The modules were delivered on 14/10/2026; on incorporation into the embedded kernel only the contract \texttt{import} was adjusted (\texttt{import TGLExt.RuleTruthContract}) and the local audit block of the originating sandbox was removed; "
             r"statements and proofs were not touched, and an \texttt{.olean} does not replace the chain's \emph{build}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The operator's four inscriptions (Luiz Antonio Rotoli Miguel, 14/10/2026), in full, embedded by sha256 (kept in the original Portuguese).} "
             + " ".join(r"\emph{``" + _v393_tex(((_V393_CUNHAGENS.get(k_) or {}).get("text") or "").strip()) + r"''} (\texttt{" + str((_vb393.get(k_) or {}).get("sha256", "AUSENTE"))[:16] + r"}.)"
                        for k_ in ("negatividade", "tetelestai", "satisfacao", "figura_da_verdade"))
             + r" The philosophical and legal readings are \textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}; the formalization that follows has its hypotheses made explicit.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The formalization, with the hypotheses.} \textsf{[REAL — Lean]} Given a faithful (injective) reading $r:N\to O$ on the space of inscriptions, a target $a:N$ and the figure $o=r(a)$, soundness $C(z)\Rightarrow r(z)=o$ and completeness "
             r"$r(z)=o\Rightarrow C(z)$ give $C(z)\leftrightarrow z=a$: the predicate is unique for that reading and that target (\texttt{sound\_complete\_eq\_admissible}, \texttt{admissible\_iff\_eq\_of\_injective}, \texttt{unique\_rule\_on\_inscriptions}). "
             r"\textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]} The clause \emph{except the figure of truth} (a gloss of ``a não ser a figura da verdade'') was represented by \emph{completeness relative to the target} --- adding no other exclusion where there is correspondence ---, a declared hypothesis, not a theorem extracted from the name. "
             r"Without completeness, rejecting everything also satisfies soundness; without a faithful reading, equal readings do not imply equal objects (fidelity holds on the subtype $\mathrm{Fix}(R)$, not on the raw space). "
             r"In the example $R(a,b)=(a,0)$, $T(a,b)=(a,e^{-1/2}b)$ the target $(1,0)$ is nonzero, the reading $R$ is an idempotent retraction and $T$ a contraction: $R(T^nx_0)=a$ already at $n=0$ and $T^nx_0\neq a$ for every finite $n$. "
             r"The link with the absolute zero is interpretation (no new thermodynamic theorem was proved) and the half-nat $e^{-1/2}$ of that example is not $\bTGL$.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The rule in the real consumer.} The numerical decision consumer (\texttt{prove\_decision\_commutation}, with its five function bodies pinned by sha256) runs at every rite; the flow "
             r"$T_t=E+e^{-\Gamma t}(\mathrm{id}-E)$ ($E$ the pinching) is evaluated against the \emph{target fixed beforehand}; the satisfaction verdict (admitted or refused) is \emph{determined} by the rule --- the reading $E(\text{state})$ against the target, within a declared numerical tolerance, "
             r"which is not exact equality ---, and the raw state and the inscription are kept in distinct fields. This round: " + _i393(_nm393.get("verificacoes")) + r" checks, " + _i393(_nm393.get("pontos")) + r" points; "
             r"the complement falls from " + _f393(_nm393.get("complemento_inicial")) + r" to " + _f393(_nm393.get("complemento_final")) + r"; the fixed space has complex dimension " + _i393(_nm393.get("dimensao_fixa_complexa"))
             + r" (uniqueness of the criterion holds for the given target, not for all fixed states); the verdict for the correct target is \texttt{" + _v393_tex(_sa393.get("veredito_do_rito")) + r"} and for the incompatible target, \texttt{" + _v393_tex(_sa393.get("veredito_incompativel")) + r"}. "
             r"Negative controls: incompatible fixed input and target refused, invalid input refused, zero rate, missing kernel evidence (each of the ten); idempotence or a global flag alone are not enough. "
             r"$\beta$ enters only as a reference rate, computed at runtime ($\alpha\sqrt e$); reference units are \textsf{[INPUT]}; finite synthetic trajectory, no observed data.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The heart and the gravitational seal.} The verdict is computed by the same rule: the reading (the verdict class obtained from the checks, from the provenance of $\chi$ and from the value of $G$) against the target fixed per source of $\chi$. "
             r"Checks: " + _i393(len(_cr393.get("checks") or [])) + r"; source of $\chi$: \texttt{" + _v393_tex(_cr393.get("chi_source")) + r"}; independent prediction: " + (r"yes" if _cr393.get("previsao_independente") else r"no") + r"; $G$ derived: " + (r"yes" if _cr393.get("G_derivado") else r"no")
             + r"; satisfaction by the rule: " + (r"admitted" if _cr_sat393.get("admitida") else r"refused") + r" (criterion " + _v393_tex(_cr_sat393.get("criterio")) + r"). "
             r"Independent spectral evidence requires a \emph{pinned chain} independent of CODATA, with the artifacts re-read by sha256: names and metadata alone do not prove origin; today the chain is \textsf{ABSENT}, and the verdict follows the reconstruction from CODATA. "
             r"The seal keeps this verdict beside the gate (\texttt{does\_not\_gate\_core}).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Limits.} The proofs do not install the dynamics in an LLM's weights, do not prove a universal legal norm and do not address nature. Validity in the kernel is not creditation, and the gate does not move. "
             r"\textsf{[DECLARED]} Reproduction caveat of the rule proof, reported by Codex: two of the three \texttt{.olean} files matched byte for byte and the concrete module had different bytes, with the same source and axioms; the cause was not determined.")
